// A function receives every argument it is given, null ones included, wherever
// they are in the list.

state
  nothing: null
  one: 1

function which(a, b)
  if a == null and b == null
    return "both null"
  if b == null
    return "last null"
  if a == null
    return "first null"
  return "none null"

beat Start
  One and nothing gives ${which(one, nothing)}.

  Nothing and nothing gives ${which(nothing, nothing)}.

  Nothing and one gives ${which(nothing, one)}.

  One and one gives ${which(one, one)}.

/*
<test>
- expected: |
    ~ One and nothing gives last null.

    ~ Nothing and nothing gives both null.

    ~ Nothing and one gives first null.

    ~ One and one gives none null.
</test>
*/
